Planetary data: NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory Development Ephemeris DE440
(Park, Folkner, Williams and Boggs, 2021), a work of the United States
government, delivered through the naif-de440 package (MIT, B612 Asteroid
Institute).

Precession and nutation: ERFA, the BSD-licensed derivative of the IAU SOFA
library, through pyerfa. File reader: jplephem (MIT, Brandon Rhodes).

Delta T before 1972: Morrison, Stephenson, Hohenkerk and Zawilski, "Addendum
2020 to Measurement of the Earth's rotation: 720 BC to AD 2015", Proc. R.
Soc. A 477 (2021), Table S15.

Fonts: Barlow and Barlow Semi Condensed by Jeremy Tribby, SIL Open Font
License 1.1. See bodygraph/fonts/OFL-barlow.txt. Text in rendered charts is
converted to outlines.

Lookup tables in bodygraph/tables.json were assembled and cross-checked from
these MIT-licensed projects:
  pyhd                        https://github.com/ppo/pyhd
  SharpAstrology.HumanDesign  https://github.com/CReizner/SharpAstrology.HumanDesign
  natalengine                 https://github.com/Unforced-Dev/natalengine
  hdkit                       https://github.com/jdempcy/hdkit

Place data: GeoNames (CC BY 4.0) through the geonamescache package.
Reference chart activations used in tests were published by Jovian Archive.

